.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_RISCV_ATTRIBUTE_VALUE_AT 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_riscv_attribute_value_at
.Nd return a parsed RISC-V attribute value by index
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn elf_riscv_attribute_value_at "const elfobj_t *obj" "size_t index"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn elf_riscv_attribute_value_at
function parses
.Pa .riscv.attributes
from
.Fa obj
and returns the integer value associated with the entry at
.Fa index .
.Pp
Some attributes may be encoded as strings in the underlying format.
Those entries do not yield a numeric payload through this accessor.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn elf_riscv_attribute_value_at
function returns the decoded integer value.
It returns 0 if
.Fa obj
is
.Dv NULL ,
if
.Fa index
is out of range,
if parsing fails,
or when the selected attribute has no numeric payload.
.Sh CAVEATS
Because 0 is also a valid numeric attribute value, callers should use
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_count 3
for range validation before indexing.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_count 3 ,
.Xr elf_riscv_attribute_tag_at 3 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
